%H A401858 Marc S. Ordower, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/31-3/ordower.pdf">The Connectivity of a Particular Graph</a>, Fibonacci Quart. 31(3) (1993), 276.
%e A401858 The only Pythagorean triangle with 3 or 4 as a side is (3, 4, 5), so a(2) = 4 and a(3) = 5.
%e A401858 The partners of 5 are 3, 4, 12 and 13, so a(4) = 12. The partners of 12 are 5, 9, 13, 15, 16, 20, 35 and 37, so a(5) = 9.
%e A401858 The only partners of 7 are 24 = a(15) and 25 = a(18), so 7 cannot occur before a(16). Since 3, 4, 5 and 6 are already used, a(16) = 7.
